### 2.1 Search Virtual Keyboard Trapping Mechanics
- **Activation**: When `SearchViewController.activate()` executes, it calls `engageTrap()` -> `SpatialNav.trap(this.keyboard)` and focuses `'Q'` (`.key-btn[data-key="Q"]`).
- **Isolation**:
  - `ArrowUp` from Row 1 (`1`, `2` ... `0`) is blocked; `SpatialNav.move('up')` returns `null` and emits `deadend`.
  - `ArrowLeft` from leftmost keys (`1`, `Q`, `A`, `CLEAR`) and `ArrowRight` from rightmost keys (`0`, `P`, `L`, `BACKSPACE`) are trapped.
  - Programmatic attempts to set focus to external elements (e.g., `SpatialNav.setFocus(headerPill)`) return `false`.
- **Controlled Escape**:
  - Pressing `ArrowDown` on action keys (`SPACE`, `CLEAR`, `DELETE`) or triggering a downward `deadend` invokes `jumpToResults()`.
  - If `#search-results-grid` contains at least one `.card-poster[data-nav="true"]`, `releaseTrap()` is called and focus transitions to `firstCard`.
  - If the results grid is empty, `jumpToResults()` aborts, keeping focus firmly trapped on the keyboard.

### 2.2 Player Modal Sheets & Error Dialog
- **Modal Lifecycle**:
  - `PlayerOSDController.openSubtitlesModal()` and `openServerModal()` dynamically render list items using pure DOM methods (`document.createElement`, `classList`, `textContent`, `setAttribute`), set `this._activeModal`, and call `SpatialNav.trap()`.
  - Focus is placed on the currently active track/server item (marked `.active`).
  - `PlayerOSDController.showError()` traps `#player-error-dialog` and focuses `#player-error-retry-btn`.
- **Hierarchical Back Key Trapping**:
  - When `this._activeModal` is non-null, pressing Back (keycode `461` or `27` / Escape) closes the modal via `closeActiveModal()`, untraps `SpatialNav`, and returns focus to the OSD button without terminating the video player.
  - A subsequent Back key press (with no active modal) gracefully exits the player back to the origin view (`#view-home`, `#view-details`, etc.).

### 2.3 Details View Overlay
- **DOM Architecture**: `#view-details` is a full-bleed view `<section id="view-details" class="view">` managed by the application router.
- **Focus Isolation**:
  - When `#view-details` is activated, `#view-home` and other views lose `.active`.
  - Under `navigation.js` line 201 (`parentView && !parentView.classList.contains('active')`), all inactive view elements are excluded from navigability.
  - Remote hammering on Details cannot bleed into inactive underlying views.

